</ul><h1>A Nice Little Boost</h1><p>Were we to offer these for the standard retail price, we’d really have to go all out.</p>
<p>We’d be pushing the whole ‘clean ingredients’ thing: the lack of preservatives, artificial sweeteners, or artificial flavors.</p>
<p>We’d be making sure that you understand that caffeine here is ‘organic.’ (Although we’re not totally clear what that means; is it from a certified organic source, or does the caffeine <em>occur</em> organically?)</p>
<p>We would use the phrase ‘plant-based’ at least six times.</p>
<p>But here’s the thing: we’re not selling this at retail price. Instead, we’re offering a 72-pack for 30 bucks. In other words, just over 40 cents per shot.</p>
<p>And because of that, we can keep it real simple. Here’s our pitch:</p>
<p>Each one offers 100mg of caffeine. Also, 120mg of L-Theanine, which apparently reduces the jitters. But, getting back to the caffeine number, we just want to clarify, that’s pretty close to the amount in a cup of coffee (give or take a few milligrams based on how strong or weak the brewer prefers it). So, it’s not like this is some ungodly payload of energy.</p>
<p>But it is enough to help you get through the workday. And we mean that even if you work for a really exhausting company. You know, one of those businesses that are known to really push their employees and customers to the limit.</p>
<p>For example:</p>
<ul>
<li>Amazon&amp;on&amp;on</li>
<li>Gruelolingo</li>
<li>TurboTaxing</li>
<li>Strain Capital</li>
<li>Capital ONErous</li>
<li>Teslaborious</li>
<li>Allstate of Torpor</li>
<li>TJ Maxxed out</li>
<li>Moving Target</li>
</ul>
<p>Yeah, wow. Are those the stupidest puns we’ve ever made or the best? To be fair, they might be both.</p>
<p>But these things we’re selling today aren’t stupid. They’re energy shots.</p>